-- seed.sql — conference ticketing test data (v3, faker-generated)
-- Built for the v2 schema: Melody's ER + group cardinality spec.
-- Deterministic: python3 gen_seed.py (seed 42). 50 venues / 50 speakers / 100 attendees / 50 events / 155 sessions / 262 registrations.
-- Insert order follows the foreign keys:
--   venues -> speakers -> attendees -> events -> sessions -> registrations
--
-- Coverage for the starter feature set (queries.py):
--   * every table has >= 10 rows (project requirement)
--   * every event has >= 1 session (contains: Event (1,N))
--   * every session has exactly one primary speaker (give: Session (1,1))
--   * 2 speakers give no session (partial participation demo): 23, 30
--   * 2 attendees never register: 99, 100
--   * 7 sessions marked 'full'
--   * 4 ticket types: VIP / Standard / Student / Sponsor
--   * statuses: confirmed / pending / cancelled
--   * (attendee_id, event_id) unique: no attendee registers twice per event
